ive response tendencies in patients with frontal brain lesions</article-title><source>Neuropsychology</source><year>2003</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>271</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12803432</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leslie</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson-Frey</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Grafton</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional imaging of face and hand imitation: towards a motor theory of empathy</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>601</fpage><lpage>607</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14980562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muthukumaraswamy</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modulation of the human mirror neuron system during cognitive activity</article-title><source>Psychophysiology</source><year>2008</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18823416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arbib</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Autism &#x02013; more than the mirror system</article-title><source>Clinical Neuropsychiatry</source><year>2007</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>208</fpage><lpage>222</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rizzolatti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallese</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Van Hemmen JL, Sejnowski TJ</surname></name></pe